{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"99516295-3962-40e1-8d55-7c7b80de287f","agentId":"afb1dbcc97469a738","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/; mes lib via cuore/services/*_bridge.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, do NOT open COM3 or call any live adapter endpoint (the car is on the bench; the main session owns it). TestClient with CUORE_STATE_DIR temp dir + fixture observations only. Minimal grepping. Report under 120 words.\n\nTonight the car was read live for the first time. The reads are stored as from-car observations in CUORE_STATE_DIR/observations.jsonl (kinds today: obd_dtcs x16, readiness x4, mode06 x1; real examples in C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl lines dated 2026-10-13 -- read a few for the exact shapes, copy them into your test fixture, do not modify that file; also docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/sessions/2026-10-13-live-read.json has the freeze-frame sweep per PID and the Mode 06 decode). Facts: MIL on, stored P0440, pending P0440+P0455, permanent P0440+P0456, all monitors complete incl. EVAP, 1663 km since clear, Mode 06 MID 3A (0.090\" leak) FAIL 404 ms vs min 3965, MID 3C one FAIL 6096 vs 6000.\n\nCorrectness bug: the Report/Bench still say \"no code has returned since the 2026-09-29 clear\" and the verdict stays UNVERIFIED_REPAIR, because cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py builds codes-returned only from MES log history + clear_assessment and ignores from-car live observations. Fix across the stack, honestly and only from-car (live_store.is_from_car) observations:\n1. dossier_bridge: a from-car obd_dtcs observation after the last clear whose stored/pending/permanent list contains a code => that code is ACTIVE (\"returned, read from the car <time>\"), the verdict becomes ACTIVE_FAULTS, MIL state shown from readiness.mil_on; the \"no code has returned\" sentence must never render when such an observation exists. Readiness from the car updates the readiness panel and the EVAP gate (monitor complete, fuel in window) -- the verdict wording: \"EVAP monitor ran and the code returned: fault is active\" not \"unverified\".\n2. Freeze frames: from-car Mode 02 reads (the sweep file shape; store them as an observation kind if the live layer already does -- check cuore/live/store.py and ops.read_freeze_frame; if freeze frames are not stored as observations today, add that in ops (record kind \"freeze_frame\" with pid/value per ECU) so the next read lands) render in the dossier/report Freeze frames section and on the Job step 5 code card and the system page, labelled \"read from the car 2026-10-13 20:03\" with the full PID list, not just the 5 MES-log fields.\n3. Mode 06: a from-car mode06 observation renders as a \"Monitor test results (Mode 06)\" block on the Report, Bench (collapsed with count: \"EVAP 0.090\\\" leak FAIL\") and the EVAP system page, with value/limit/pass per MID+TID; and each failing EVAP MID becomes an evidence item the hypothesis ledger can attach (kind \"measurement\", label 'Mode 06 EVAP 0.090\" leak: FAIL 404 ms vs min 3965 ms (car, 2026-10-13)'), offered in the step-7 evidence picker and auto-suggested on the EVAP hypotheses' \"evidence for\" (not auto-attached; the mechanic attaches). Bench next-action sentence should now say the monitor has run and the large-leak test failed, next: Test A (hand vacuum on the ESIM while watching the switch PID).\n4. Tests surface: the row for \"evap_smoke\" must not be marked by this; instead add a read-only \"From the car\" strip at the top of /v/{vin}/tests listing the Mode 06 EVAP results with date.\nTests: cuore/tests/check_live_ingest.py (new): with the fixture observations, dossier verdict == ACTIVE_FAULTS, P0440 ACTIVE with the from-car wording, no \"no code has returned\" text on Report/Bench, freeze frame block shows fuel_level 28.6 and commanded_evap_purge 18.0, Mode 06 block shows the 3A FAIL, the evidence picker on Job step 7 lists the Mode 06 item, Bench next action mentions Test A; without the fixture nothing changes (run check_bench.py, check_dossier_page.py or check_screens.py, check_jobs_page.py, check_tests_page.py, check_job_ux.py)."},"uuid":"bc63b9e1-358d-4088-862a-f761d9cac0d4","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:18:12.536Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
