{"parentUuid":"665441f7-b245-42f8-95f6-186dc779c3d6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afb1dbcc97469a738","attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"Scope addition for the live-read ingestion: a UDS sweep tonight produced module codes that must reach the verdict and the dossier too. A new observation kind \"module_dtcs\" {ecu, bus, dtcs: [{code: \"U1713-2F\", raw, status: 15, flags: {testFailed, pendingDTC, confirmedDTC, testFailedSinceLastClear, testNotCompletedThisOperationCycle, warningIndicatorRequested, ...}}]} will be recorded by a full-scan module another agent is writing; tonight's real values: ECM P0440-00 status 205, P0455-00 status 77; BCM U1765-86 8, U1736-87 8, U1713-2F 15, B1176-97 8, B10AA-4A 8; IPC U1736-86 12, U1736-87 12; RFHUB B1040-64 8; TCM none. Rules: a code with confirmedDTC or testFailed or pendingDTC is ACTIVE on that module; testFailedSinceLastClear only (status 8) is HISTORY (\"failed since last clear, not failing now\"); testNotCompletedThisOperationCycle only (status 64) is NOT RUN and never listed as a fault. Fold these into dossier_bridge the same way as obd_dtcs (per-code state with module name and the from-car time), into the network/body families the code-family logic already knows (three or more lost-communication codes = one bus event), and into the verdict (any ACTIVE module code = ACTIVE_FAULTS even if Mode 03 were clean). Add fixture cases to check_live_ingest.py: U1713-2F active on BCM, B1176-97 history, status-64 codes absent from every list.","source_uuid":"56d70bde-f00d-4a86-a01e-efb059e5d7dd","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"isMeta":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"01e8c480-6105-4903-9366-8881758d229b","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:28:03.509Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe coordinator sent a message while you were working:\nScope addition for the live-read ingestion: a UDS sweep tonight produced module codes that must reach the verdict and the dossier too. A new observation kind \"module_dtcs\" {ecu, bus, dtcs: [{code: \"U1713-2F\", raw, status: 15, flags: {testFailed, pendingDTC, confirmedDTC, testFailedSinceLastClear, testNotCompletedThisOperationCycle, warningIndicatorRequested, ...}}]} will be recorded by a full-scan module another agent is writing; tonight's real values: ECM P0440-00 status 205, P0455-00 status 77; BCM U1765-86 8, U1736-87 8, U1713-2F 15, B1176-97 8, B10AA-4A 8; IPC U1736-86 12, U1736-87 12; RFHUB B1040-64 8; TCM none. Rules: a code with confirmedDTC or testFailed or pendingDTC is ACTIVE on that module; testFailedSinceLastClear only (status 8) is HISTORY (\"failed since last clear, not failing now\"); testNotCompletedThisOperationCycle only (status 64) is NOT RUN and never listed as a fault. Fold these into dossier_bridge the same way as obd_dtcs (per-code state with module name and the from-car time), into the network/body families the code-family logic already knows (three or more lost-communication codes = one bus event), and into the verdict (any ACTIVE module code = ACTIVE_FAULTS even if Mode 03 were clean). Add fixture cases to check_live_ingest.py: U1713-2F active on BCM, B1176-97 history, status-64 codes absent from every list.\n\nAddress this before completing your current task.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
