{"parentUuid":"a6443f38-9b8a-41d9-8e01-ffb882d7f2fa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b6cd0a50-3b6c-4dd3-978a-0b81b352eabb","agentId":"afb1dbcc97469a738","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1s5Yd5qt8vLfVeEoRSmhs","type":"tool_result","content":"8516 flow-step-why muted small\">no hypothesis recorded yet, and t\r\n9398 7\" class=\"flow-step-title\">7. Hypotheses</a>\r\n               \r\n9491 flow-step-why muted small\">no hypothesis recorded yet</span>\r\n14643 N5J7B88115/job?step=7\" title=\"Hypotheses\"\r\n       aria-curren\r\n14743 \"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypotheses\"><use href=\"/static\r\n14804 icons.svg?v=3d2dcbe0c9#i-step_hypothesis\"></use></svg></span\r\n23698 =\"step-headline-why small\">no hypothesis recorded yet, and t\r\n24377 \"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypothesis\"><use href=\"/static\r\n24438 icons.svg?v=3d2dcbe0c9#i-step_hypothesis\"></use></svg></span\r\n24556 n class=\"step-headline-title\">Hypotheses</span>\r\n    <span cl\r\n24619 =\"step-headline-why small\">no hypothesis recorded yet</span>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8cc832c0-c2c8-4315-9989-2a12183456c0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:43:12.683Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"8516 flow-step-why muted small\">no hypothesis recorded yet, and t\r\n9398 7\" class=\"flow-step-title\">7. Hypotheses</a>\r\n               \r\n9491 flow-step-why muted small\">no hypothesis recorded yet</span>\r\n14643 N5J7B88115/job?step=7\" title=\"Hypotheses\"\r\n       aria-curren\r\n14743 \"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypotheses\"><use href=\"/static\r\n14804 icons.svg?v=3d2dcbe0c9#i-step_hypothesis\"></use></svg></span\r\n23698 =\"step-headline-why small\">no hypothesis recorded yet, and t\r\n24377 \"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypothesis\"><use href=\"/static\r\n24438 icons.svg?v=3d2dcbe0c9#i-step_hypothesis\"></use></svg></span\r\n24556 n class=\"step-headline-title\">Hypotheses</span>\r\n    <span cl\r\n24619 =\"step-headline-why small\">no hypothesis recorded yet</span>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":7,"newStart":34,"newLines":43,"lines":[" Do **not** clear any codes before Test A is run and recorded (see Safety,"," below). Clearing destroys the very evidence Test A and the verdict need."," ","-## 1. The exact MCP calls, in order","+## 1. The fast path: `full_scan()`, then Test A","+","+Run **`full_scan(vin=\"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\")`** once. It performs the whole","+read-only capture in section 2 below in a single call -- verify, VIN, every","+DTC status plus freeze frame for every PID the car actually supports,","+readiness, Mode 06, a Mode 01 snapshot, and a UDS sweep (DTCs, identity, a","+short known-DID list) on every bus the declared cable reaches -- and","+records every reading as an observation through","+`cuore.live.store.record_observation`, so the Scans area, the dossier and","+the health report all see it without the manual calls below. Its result is","+a coverage summary: which bus/module answered, which was silent, and which","+was not reachable and why (`\"needs grey A6 cable\"`, `\"no known address: run","+discovery\"`, an NRC, ...). Check that summary before trusting anything","+else: a module marked `not_reachable` for a fixable reason (wrong cable,","+needs discovery) is worth a second pass first.","+","+After `full_scan()`:","+- Drive or idle through the fuel window (step 11 in section 2), then call","+  `read_readiness()` again and compare -- `full_scan()` is a one-shot","+  baseline, not a monitor; there is no substitute for the second readiness","+  read.","+- Run **Test A** (step 15 in section 2) with wiTECH or MultiEcuScan --","+  `full_scan()` does not run actuator tests.","+- `read_fullscan_last()` returns the same coverage summary again without","+  re-running the scan, if you need to recheck it later in the session.","+","+`full_scan()` refuses outright (no partial scan, nothing recorded) while","+MultiEcuScan holds the port, or a live-data poll session (step 8 in section","+2) is running -- stop the poller (`live_session_stop()`) or disconnect MES","+first, same as every call below.","+","+## 2. The manual sequence (fallback)","+","+Use this when `full_scan()` cannot run (MES needs the port for something","+else, or one step needs to be repeated or inspected on its own) -- it is","+the same reads, one call at a time, in the same order `full_scan()` runs","+them."," "," Each step names the tool, what it proves, and which cuore page should show"," the result afterward."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ee0cbe5d-3ad8-45f0-bd34-76bbe0560b34","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a6443f38-9b8a-41d9-8e01-ffb882d7f2fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
